# Testing & Logging

## Testing strategy — pragmatic for MVP

Test what matters. Don't test boilerplate.

| Layer | Tool | When runs | What to test |
|-------|------|-----------|-------------|
| Unit | Pytest + Jest | Every branch push | Core business logic |
| Component | React Testing Library | Every PR | Critical UI components |
| Integration | Pytest | Every PR | Critical API endpoints |
| E2E | Playwright | Merge to main | 5 critical scenarios only |

### Critical paths that MUST have tests

**Python unit tests:**
- Instruction layer assembly — all five levels merge correctly
- Workflow engine sequencing — threads execute in order, task memory passes forward
- RAG retrieval — threshold logic, fallback, four-level priority
- Structured output validation — Pydantic schemas reject invalid JSON
- Intervention trigger detection — correct pause conditions
- Model routing rules — correct model returned per thread type and budget state

**Integration tests:**
- `POST /api/v1/tasks` — creates task with correct module type
- `POST /api/v1/tasks/{id}/threads` — creates thread, triggers structured Q&A
- `POST /api/v1/documents/upload` — document queued for processing
- `POST /api/v1/workflows/{id}/execute` — workflow starts, returns execution ID
- `GET /api/v1/tasks/{id}/memory` — returns task memory in correct grouped structure

### 5 Playwright E2E scenarios — these are the critical paths

```typescript
// tests/e2e/scenarios.spec.ts

// Scenario 1: Core task/thread flow
test("researcher creates task, uploads paper, opens thread, receives AI response", ...)

// Scenario 2: Student paper review workflow
test("professor creates assignment, adds submission, runs automated workflow, views output", ...)

// Scenario 3: Hebrew language flow
test("task created in Hebrew, AI responds in Hebrew, RTL layout correct", ...)

// Scenario 4: Word export
test("thread output exported to Word document, file downloads correctly", ...)

// Scenario 5: Workflow intervention
test("workflow pauses on intervention trigger, user responds, workflow resumes", ...)
```

## Structured logging — always use this pattern

**NEVER use `print()`. NEVER use Python's default `logging` module directly.**

All logging goes through the structured logger in `core/logging.py`:

```python
# core/logging.py
import structlog

logger = structlog.get_logger()

# Usage — always include relevant IDs for traceability
logger.info("event_name", key="value", another_key="value")
```

### Required log events — log ALL of these

```python
# AI calls
logger.info("ai_call_start", thread_id=..., model_id=..., thread_type=..., instruction_version=...)
logger.info("ai_call_complete", thread_id=..., input_tokens=..., output_tokens=..., cached_tokens=..., latency_ms=...)
logger.warning("ai_call_failed", thread_id=..., error=..., retry_count=...)

# RAG retrieval  
logger.info("rag_retrieval", query_hash=..., chunks_retrieved=..., threshold_used=..., latency_ms=...)

# Workflow execution
logger.info("workflow_started", workflow_id=..., task_id=..., thread_count=...)
logger.info("workflow_thread_complete", workflow_id=..., thread_type=..., memory_entries_written=...)
logger.info("workflow_intervention", workflow_id=..., trigger_type=..., thread_type=...)
logger.info("workflow_complete", workflow_id=..., total_threads=..., total_tokens=..., total_cost_usd=...)

# Document processing
logger.info("document_upload", document_id=..., file_type=..., size_bytes=...)
logger.info("document_processed", document_id=..., chunks_created=..., processing_ms=...)
logger.warning("document_processing_failed", document_id=..., error=...)

# User actions
logger.info("task_created", task_id=..., module_type=..., user_id=...)
logger.info("thread_opened", thread_id=..., task_id=..., thread_type=...)
logger.info("report_exported", task_id=..., format=...)

# Errors — always log with context
logger.error("unhandled_error", error=str(e), context=relevant_context)
```

### Log format — always JSON in production

```python
# core/logging.py
import structlog
import logging
import sys

def configure_logging():
    structlog.configure(
        processors=[
            structlog.contextvars.merge_contextvars,
            structlog.processors.add_log_level,
            structlog.processors.TimeStamper(fmt="iso"),
            structlog.processors.JSONRenderer(),
        ],
        wrapper_class=structlog.make_filtering_bound_logger(logging.INFO),
        logger_factory=structlog.PrintLoggerFactory(file=sys.stdout),
    )
```

## What NOT to log
- ❌ Never log paper content or document text
- ❌ Never log student names or personal data
- ❌ Never log API keys, tokens, or secrets
- ❌ Never log full AI prompts (log prompt hash + length instead)
- ❌ Never log full AI responses (log response length + structured output schema)
